  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\n\nThe overall synoptic pattern will remain the same throughout the\nweekend with a ridge of high pressure locked over the\nsoutheastern states and rounds of shortwave energy tracking over\nthe periphery of the ridge. With progressively saturated soils\nafter days of continued rainfall, flash flooding will remain a\nthreat across the region. The Weather Prediction Center\ncurrently places at least some portions of the area under a\nSlight Risk of Excessive Rainfall each day through 12Z Monday.\nPrecipitable water values will remain high during this entire\nperiod, ranging from 2.00 to 2.25 inches.\n\nThe pattern will begin to shift early next week. On Tuesday, the\naxis of the upper-level ridge will transition from the\nsoutheastern states to the southwestern states, and a surface \nhigh will build into the middle Ohio Valley and Appalachians.\nThis would bring the return of some drier weather area-wide\nTuesday and Wednesday, before another system approaches later in\nthe week with rain returning.",
